# shadcn/ui Components

## Resolution order

1. Look in `src/renderer/src/components/ui/` - it may already be installed.
2. Check the shadcn registry and run `npx shadcn@latest add <name>`.
3. Only if neither covers it, build the component - and say why first.

Writing a `Dialog`, `Select`, `Popover`, or `Table` by hand is not acceptable.
These are in the registry, and hand-rolled versions lose the Radix
accessibility behaviour (focus trapping, keyboard nav, ARIA wiring).

## Compose, do not fork

Treat `components/ui/` as generated code. To specialise a primitive, wrap it
rather than editing it, so `shadcn` can still update the original.

```tsx
// GOOD - a wrapper in components/, composing the primitive
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

export function SubmitButton({ pending, ...props }: SubmitButtonProps) {
  return <Button type="submit" disabled={pending} {...props} />
}
```

Editing `components/ui/` directly is fine only for project-wide token or
variant changes that every consumer should inherit.

## Class names and variants

- Merge conditional classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`, never template
  strings, so later Tailwind utilities win conflicts predictably.
- Express variants with `cva`, not branching ternaries on `className`.

```tsx
// BAD
<div className={`p-4 ${isActive ? 'bg-accent' : ''}`} />

// GOOD
<div className={cn('p-4', isActive && 'bg-accent')} />
```
